    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nExtended 4 bedroom Period house of c. 129 sqm just off the Battery Road on the outskirts of Longford town centre.\n\nThe house was originally built in the 1920's but has been extensively modernised and is presented in excellent condition with a stylish décor. \n\nThe house features a living room with a solid fuel insert stove that has a back boiler and solid wood floors. The kitchen is to the rear of the house has walnut wood built in units with appliances and polished porcelain tiled floors. Off the kitchen there is a utility area with a WC & WHB. The dining room also has polished porcelain tiled floors and an open fireplace. \n\nUpstairs the main bedroom is very spacious with beautiful solid wood floors. There is a family sized shower room semi tiled. Ther are two more double sized bedrooms and a single sized bedroom, that would be an ideal home office to take advantage of the high speed fibre broadband available in the area. \n\n\nServices:\n• Mains Water and Sewerage, \n• Dual System central heating (Oil boiler and back boiler on stove)\n• Fibre to the home & Cablecom Gigabyte high speed broadband available.\n\n\nOutside: \nThe house is elevated from the road with pedestrian steps leading to the front door surrounded by a small garden. \n\nThere is an access lane along the side of the house leading to the rear garden and the parking for at least two cars. Behind this is a paved patio area and garden of lawns and mature planting and hedges affording privacy. There is a metal garden shed and a lean to storage area.\n\n\nLocation:\nThe house is ideally located just off Longford's much sought after Battery Road, within easy walking distance of the town centre. \n\nSurrounded be a vast array of sporting amenities being beside Pearce Park GAA grounds & close to Longford Rugby Club. The house is convenient to the N4 Dublin Sligo Rd and the Axis retail park beside it. There is a local shop at a petrol service just two minutes walk away on the Battery Road. Yet a few minutes walk down the Lisbrack road in the opposite direction finds you in the middle of agricultural lands and quiet country roads. \n\n\nEircode: N39 Y6W2 \nGPS: 53.7381, -7.8029"
      },
